1
00:00:00,072 --> 00:00:02,452
(Amy:)...to use the clinical term, bitchiness...

2
00:00:04,243 --> 00:00:06,913
(Amy:)...is because your mother
isn't making you a priority?

3
00:00:07,079 --> 00:00:11,169
No. Or to use the clinical term: Nuh-uh.

4
00:00:12,751 --> 00:00:14,841
(Amy:)Are you sure?
The infant-mother pair-bond...

5
00:00:15,003 --> 00:00:16,333
(Amy:)...is the building block
of primate psychology.

6
00:00:16,505 --> 00:00:19,385
(Sheldon:)Oh, there it is. It always comes back
to monkeys with you.

7
00:00:19,550 --> 00:00:21,590
(Sheldon:)Just monkeys, monkeys, monkeys.

8
00:00:22,553 --> 00:00:24,383
(Amy:)Sheldon, we're all animals.

9
00:00:24,555 --> 00:00:27,185
(Amy:)There are aspects of you
that are extraordinary...

10
00:00:27,349 --> 00:00:30,939
...but when it comes to relationships,
you're like everybody else.

11
00:00:31,103 --> 00:00:33,733
(Sheldon:)Are you trying to suggest
that my emotional problems...

12
00:00:33,897 --> 00:00:36,987
(Sheldon:)...are no different
than those of a stupid person?

13
00:00:37,943 --> 00:00:40,863
(Amy:)Actually, some research indicates
that by not overthinking...

14
00:00:41,029 --> 00:00:43,279
(Amy:)...the less intelligent
handle emotions better.

15
00:00:45,993 --> 00:00:47,873
(Amy:)Sure you're not coming down
with a cold?

16
00:00:48,036 --> 00:00:50,786
(Sheldon:)Oh, yes, the common cold.
Just like everyone else.

17
00:00:50,998 --> 00:00:53,038
(Sheldon:)You'd love that, wouldn't you?

18
00:00:55,544 --> 00:00:57,794
(Mrs Cooper:)Oh, this one's sweet.

19
00:00:57,963 --> 00:01:01,023
(Mrs Cooper:)You know, for your rosary rattlers.

